.TH KLDCTL 1 "JANUARY 2026" "0.0.1-kneecap" "Kaleidux Manual"
.SH NAME
kldctl \- Control utility for the Kaleidux wallpaper daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kldctl
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kldctl
is the primary interface for interacting with a running
.B kaleidux-daemon
instance. It uses a Unix domain socket to send commands for wallpaper switching, playlist management, and status queries.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-s, \-\-socket \fI<SOCKET>\fR
Path to the daemon's Unix socket. Defaults to \fIXDG_RUNTIME_DIR/kaleidux.sock\fR or \fI/tmp/kaleidux-{USER}.sock\fR.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Show version information.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print help information.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B jump PATH [-o OUTPUT]
Display an image inside the slideshow directory using the normal transition and history.
.TP
.B set PATH [-o OUTPUT]
Insert an image into the current in-memory queue and advance to it immediately.
.TP
.B img PATH [-o OUTPUT]
Select a slideshow image or insert an external image and display it. Existing entries are not duplicated. Relative paths use the client working directory. All three commands accept images only and honor output groups; omitted output targets all outputs. Queue rebuilds can discard external entries.
.TP
.B status \fR(alias: \fBst\fR)
Display the current status of the daemon, including active wallpapers and playback state.
.TP
.B next \fR(alias: \fBn\fR)
Force the daemon to skip to the next wallpaper in the queue.
.TP
.B prev \fR(alias: \fBp\fR)
Switch back to the previously displayed wallpaper if history is available.
.TP
.B love \fI<PATH>\fR [\fI-m MULTIPLIER\fR]
Mark the specified file as "loved", increasing its selection frequency in the "loveit" sorting strategy.
.TP
.B unlove \fI<PATH>\fR
Remove the love status from a file, resetting its selection weight.
.TP
.B lovelist \fR(alias: \fBll\fR)
List all files currently in the love list.
.TP
.B pause
Pause video playback and automatic wallpaper rotation independently of named inhibitors.
.TP
.B resume
Clear manual pause. Playback remains paused while named inhibitors are active.
.TP
.B inhibit \fI<REASON>\fR
Inhibit wallpaper playback and rotation with a named reason. Playback remains paused as long as any inhibitor is active or manual pause is engaged.
.TP
.B uninhibit \fI<REASON>\fR
Remove a named pause inhibitor. Removing an inhibitor will not resume playback if other inhibitors or manual pause remain active.
.TP
.B inhibitors \fR[\fBlist\fR]
List all currently active pause inhibitors.
Names are case-sensitive, at most 64 UTF-8 bytes, nonblank, and cannot contain control characters. Up to 64 names may be active. Duplicate acquisition is idempotent, not reference-counted. Reasons remain until released or the daemon exits; they do not expire when the calling process exits.
.TP
.B clear \fR[\fI-o OUTPUT\fR]
Clear wallpaper on the specified output or all outputs.
.TP
.B query \fR(alias: \fBq\fR)
Query connected outputs and their current content state.
.TP
.B reload
Request the daemon to reload its configuration file from disk.
.TP
.B kill
Instruct the daemon to shut down gracefully.
.TP
.B playlist \fI<SUBCOMMAND>\fR
Manage content playlists. Subcommands include: \fBcreate\fR, \fBadd\fR, \fBremove\fR, \fBload\fR, \fBlist\fR, \fBdelete\fR.
.TP
.B blacklist \fI<SUBCOMMAND>\fR
Manage the blacklist of files to exclude from rotation. Subcommands include: \fBadd\fR, \fBremove\fR, \fBlist\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success. Connection failures, invalid arguments, and errors reported by the daemon return a nonzero status.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kaleidux-daemon (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mjoyufull <https://github.com/Mjoyufull/Kaleidux>
